        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-11-04 08:33:43.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. This needs a refresh: the converted code can't build when CONFIG_LUSTRE_FS_SERVER=m, because the shared headers in lustre/include/ still use #ifdef. Also, the ldlm/ objects that are linked into ptlrpc.ko (ldlm_lockd.c, ldlm_lib.c, ldlm_lock.c, ldlm_flock.c, ldlm_internal.h, ...) still use #ifdef CONFIG_LUSTRE_FS_SERVER. With =m the same module would get server-side ptlrpc and target code but client-only ldlm. Should ldlm/ and the headers be converted in this patch, or in an earlier one in the series?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
